        "text": "TASK 329 • DK1 RESULTS • SOURCE eb5aa13 • PRESENTATION ONLY\nA supplied non-rest proxy raises the clean-gate count to 7/9.\n\nSame three takes and seeds: the earlier release-from-rest proxy was 0/9 clean. The 18° proxy changes initial velocity, motion extent and measurement visibility together.\n\nAttributed provisional result from dk1. Source-file and playback checks here add no independent physics measurement.\n\nEvery attempt stays in the denominator\nProxy arm\tClean\tClean + within 10% of P\tAccepted ACF median ×P\nHistorical release-from-rest\t0/9\t0/9\t—\nSupplied 18° + P\t7/9\t7/9\t0.994\nSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t4/9\t0/9\t1.671\n\nThree takes × three seeds. Each new arm has 9 clips. No new plain arm was generated. Accepted-only ACF interval [0.992122, 1.001472] resamples seven selected rows; it is not scene-general uncertainty.\n\nPeriod, amplitude and direction are supplied. P comes from later real video; 18° and inward direction are assumptions. This does not demonstrate a first-frame-only recipe. Review #6738/#6753 challenges amplitude-only causation: rendered motion, reader visibility, or both may explain the gate gain.\n\nPlay the three source-native examples\n\nOne committed first available seed per take, all source-clean. These examples are selected, not the full experiment. Bob deformation was reported by the author and was not scored.\n\nExample \nreal_09 · seed 1\nreal_14 · seed 101\nreal_16 · seed 1\n\nOpen native MP4 · 832×480, 93 frames at 24 fps. No compositing or retiming here.\n\nThe three source inputs\nreal_09: supplied P=1.172700s; new main arm 2/3 clean.\nreal_14: supplied P=1.187767s; new main arm 3/3 clean.\nreal_16: supplied P=1.187400s; new main arm 2/3 clean.\nNumerical control and gate acceptance are different\n\nThe wrong-period ×1.7 arm follows the longer target numerically on both readers in 9/9 attempts. Only 4/9 pass the frozen gate; five remain rejected with ACF check. This 9/9 observation is ungated.\n\nTwo main-arm outputs are rejected for reader disagreement: real_09 seed 2 and real_16 seed 3. Another accepted row, real_09 seed 3, has MP flag check and R² 0.265. The frozen gate does not require the MP flag or a minimum R².\n\nAll 18 saved outcomes\n\nRatios divide each saved reader period by the supplied P, including rejected outputs. They are display calculations, not new tracking.\n\nTake \nAll takes\nreal_09\nreal_14\nreal_16\nArm \nBoth arms\nSupplied 18° + P\nSupplied 18° + 1.7P\n\n18 saved rows\n\nTake\tArm\tSeed\tFrozen gate\tACF/P\tACF flag\tMP/P\tMP flag\tMP R²\tFlicker\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + P\t1\tPASS\t1.001\tok\t1.002\tok\t0.99\t0.0068\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + P\t2\tREJECT\t0.989\tok\t2.548\tcheck\t0.22\t0.0060\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + P\t3\tPASS\t0.994\tok\t0.931\tcheck\t0.27\t0.0079\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t1\tPASS\t1.672\tok\t1.685\tcheck\t1.00\t0.0069\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t2\tPASS\t1.670\tok\t1.694\tok\t0.99\t0.0059\nreal_09\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t3\tPASS\t1.691\tok\t1.679\tok\t0.99\t0.0081\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + P\t101\tPASS\t1.001\tok\t1.003\tok\t0.99\t0.0058\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + P\t102\tPASS\t0.988\tok\t0.996\tok\t0.99\t0.0064\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + P\t103\tPASS\t0.992\tok\t0.999\tok\t0.99\t0.0047\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t101\tPASS\t1.670\tok\t1.703\tcheck\t0.99\t0.0057\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t102\tREJECT\t1.699\tcheck\t1.713\tok\t0.99\t0.0061\nreal_14\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t103\tREJECT\t1.755\tcheck\t1.730\tok\t0.99\t0.0049\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + P\t1\tPASS\t0.993\tok\t0.998\tok\t1.00\t0.0063\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + P\t2\tPASS\t1.009\tok\t1.008\tok\t0.99\t0.0057\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + P\t3\tREJECT\t1.004\tok\t0.495\tcheck\t0.32\t0.0074\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t1\tREJECT\t1.760\tcheck\t1.757\tcheck\t1.00\t0.0064\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t2\tREJECT\t1.716\tcheck\t1.704\tcheck\t0.99\t0.0058\nreal_16\tSupplied 18° + 1.7P\t3\tREJECT\t1.689\tcheck\t1.688\tcheck\t1.00\t0.0074\nFrozen rule, uncertainty and calibration\nThe author's complete contact sheets\nSheet \nSupplied 18° + P\nSupplied 18° + 1.7P\nUnchanged author sheets: real_09, real_14, real_16; three seeds per take and eight cropped/resized frames per row. Author labels retain rejections. Static sheets are not a playback test. Only the three committed native clips above are packaged; hashes and sidecars cover all 18.\nKeep the claim within this evidence\nThe gate improvement supports the whole supplied non-rest proxy package on these clips. It does not identify amplitude as the sole cause or establish general scene transfer.\nSupplied P uses later-video timing (assumed 25 Hz); amplitude/direction and manual geometry are extra inputs. One still pose does not determine angular velocity.\nNo NVIDIA-scoreboard check for these 18 clips. The separate quality scorecard reports ~0.057 DOVER cost on another cohort. Plausibility, robot prediction and non-regression remain unproved.\nLow luminance flicker does not certify stable shape. Some bob deformation is reported and unscored. Default changes belong to recipe owners; none are applied here.\nGeneration settings and sampler provenance\nPresentation readout\nSaved results\nFrozen analyzer\nOriginal job builder\nByte receipts\nFinding and challenges\nHistorical 276\nHistorical 277\nPinned original source\nEarlier fresh-input demo",
